WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.080
SPEAKER 1: My son played very
serious soccer when he was younger.

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:08.340
And at one point, he got a condition
called Osgood Schlatter, which

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:12.540
is essentially something that happens
when you're athletic and you grow.

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:14.220
He couldn't walk.

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:19.080
So we went to the pediatrician, who
pushed on his knee, he screamed.

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:22.680
And the pediatrician said,
he's got Osgood Schlatter.

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:25.890
Wait several weeks, he'll get better.

00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:29.310
So we waited like two days.

00:00:29.310 --> 00:00:33.690
And then someone told us that we
should go to see a specialist.

00:00:33.690 --> 00:00:36.900
So we went into MGH to see a specialist.

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:41.100
The specialist pushed on his knee in
the exact right place, my son screamed.

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:44.430
The specialist said, he
has Osgood Schlatter.

00:00:44.430 --> 00:00:48.370
But maybe we should get an MRI to
make sure nothing else is going on.

00:00:48.370 --> 00:00:51.910
So we took him out to the
MRI machine up on Route 128.

00:00:51.910 --> 00:00:53.040
He got the MRI.

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:53.880
We got the image.

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:55.200
We went back to the specialist.

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:58.050
The specialist looked at the
image and the specialist said,

00:00:58.050 --> 00:00:59.250
he has Osgood Schlatter.

00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:00.510
Everything else is fine.

00:01:00.510 --> 00:01:02.940
Wait a few weeks and he'll get better.

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:04.709
So we waited a bit longer.

00:01:04.709 --> 00:01:08.700
And his soccer coach said, you need
to go see the sports medicine doctor

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:09.990
at Children's.

00:01:09.990 --> 00:01:12.900
So we took him in to the
sports medicine doctor.

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:17.280
The sports medicine doctor
pressed on his knee, he screamed.

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:21.030
The sports medicine doctor
said, he has Osgood Schlatter.

00:01:21.030 --> 00:01:23.430
Wait a few weeks and he'll be better.

00:01:23.430 --> 00:01:25.950
But by now we were kind
of in a few weeks anyway,

00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:28.230
we only had to wait a little bit longer.

00:01:28.230 --> 00:01:33.930
And true enough, a few weeks later, he
was actually better and all was good.

00:01:33.930 --> 00:01:36.270
But all that consumption--

00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:40.290
Passed the first pediatrician visit,
the specialist visit, the MRI,

00:01:40.290 --> 00:01:44.280
the second specialist visit, the
visit to the sports medicine person.

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:49.200
All those things were probably
visits we might not have done

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:51.700
had we actually had to pay.

00:01:51.700 --> 00:01:54.240
So all of that consumption
probably would fit

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:56.160
under the category of moral hazard--

00:01:56.160 --> 00:01:59.500
Things that we did because it was free.

